## System Architecture

The ATM Machine Simulation System follows a modular architecture. The main program controls the application flow and connects the ATM menu with authentication, account management, transactions, transaction history, validation, and account data storage.

### Architecture Flow

main.py
↓
atm.py
↓
├── authentication.py → Login and PIN verification
├── account.py → Account creation, details, and PIN change
├── transactions.py → Deposit, withdrawal, balance, and transfer
├── transaction_history.py → Transaction history
└── validation.py → Input validation
↓
database.py → Stores account and transaction data


## Workflow Diagram

The workflow describes the sequence of operations performed by the user from opening the ATM system to logging out. The user can create an account or log in and then access the available ATM operations.


### Use Case Diagram

The Use Case Diagram shows the interaction between the user and the ATM Machine Simulation System. The user can create an account, log in, and perform banking operations such as checking balance, depositing money, withdrawing money, transferring money, viewing account details, viewing transaction history, changing the PIN, and logging out.


### Class Diagram

The Class Diagram represents the main components of the ATM Machine Simulation System and the operations handled by each component. It shows how account management, account data, transactions, and transaction history are organized within the system.


### Sequence Diagram

The Sequence Diagram shows the interaction between the user and the main components of the ATM Machine Simulation System during login and an ATM operation. It represents the sequence of communication between the main program, authentication, ATM menu, transaction processing, and account data.


### Data Structure Diagram

The Data Structure Diagram represents the account information maintained by the ATM system. Each account contains an account number, name, PIN, balance, and transaction records. The transaction records store activities such as deposits, withdrawals, and transfers.
